    "explanation": "To both parties: the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee is refunded to the rider in full.\n\nFor the rider: your core point is upheld. Under POL-NS-02 the driver is deemed to have arrived only if the GPS trace carries at least three consecutive fixes inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius at 25 m accuracy or better. The driver's own trace (EV-GPS-00212) reports qualifying_fix_count 0 and a longest qualifying in-geofence run of 0.0 s across the fifteen minutes before the 08:20:30 cancellation. His closest approach was 37.94 m from the pin, i.e. inside the 50 m radius, but that fix did not clear the 25 m accuracy filter, and POL-NS-02 provides that accuracy-filtered fixes count as evidence of neither presence nor absence. With no qualifying in-radius fix anywhere in the window, POL-NS-01 limb (b) fails and the fee is not chargeable. The waiting-period arithmetic is the same story: the required dwell for a STANDARD pickup is 300 s (POL-NS-01 limb (c); POL-NS-06), the measured in-geofence dwell is 0 s and the shortfall is 300 s, so POL-NS-06 makes the fee non-chargeable whether or not you were present. The fare line refunded is the cancellation-fee line of SGD 4.00 in fare_breakdown (total_charged SGD 4.00, payment_status CHARGED, nothing yet refunded).\n\nFor the driver: your claims that POL-NS-01 limbs (a) and (d) are met are accepted (the trip record carries an 'arrived' event at 08:12:35 and terminates by you with EXCESSIVE_WAIT, not DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE), as is your point that the anti-farming check does not trip and that the fare reconciles. But the clause is conjunctive and fails at (b) and (c), and two of your arguments do not move the outcome. POL-NS-03 does not govern: it applies only where the trace shows you stationary for the required dwell within 400 m of the pin, and your own trace shows movement across the window - 3.2 km travelled, speeds of 25.2 and 43.5 km/h, and a maximum distance of 1082 m from the pin - so a mean distance of 294.05 m does not establish a parked position inside the 400 m corridor. Even if it did, POL-NS-03 would still refund the fee and would award you nothing, because the rider named Exit A in the chat log (POL-NS-03(i)) and registered_pickup_points is 1, so the pin-ambiguity goodwill route (POL-NS-03(ii), needing 2 or more) is unavailable. Driver compensation is therefore nil: POL-NS-07 pays only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it, and that is not this case. The 80% figure of SGD 3.20 you cite is simply never reached, and POL-NS-09(d) is not engaged (2 terminations, below 4; 2/132 = 0.015, below 0.08).\n\nOn the contested rider claim that the 08:12:35 marker is a FALSE arrival under POL-NS-05 and that limb (ii) should record a false-arrival event against the driver: that is not made out. POL-NS-05 turns on a single GPS fix matched to the arrival timestamp showing the driver more than 300 m from the pin, or travelling at 15 km/h or above; the derived trace publishes no arrival-matched fix and leaves dwell_start_offset_sec null, so the test cannot be run on this record. The refund follows from POL-NS-02 and POL-NS-06, not from POL-NS-05, and no false-arrival referral issues.\n\nOther matters: POL-NS-04 does not apply, because the rider's locating message at 08:15:02 was answered by the driver at 08:15:30, inside the 120 s window. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00212-01 is MISSING, with a null payload and weight 0.0; its absence is citable but it can carry no fact, so POL-NS-06(i) accumulation is unavailable and the 300 s shortfall stands unreduced.\n\nNo escalation. Confidence is 0.85, above the 0.70 floor. No POL-NS-08(a)-(d) impairment: there is no clock skew (the 08:12:35 arrival sits within 5 s of a fix on the 10 s cadence, and acceptance and termination times match), no trace gap (93 fixes, maximum gap 0.0 s) and the rider track is present, the chat log holds all four messages in sequence with no five-minute gap, and the SGD 4.00 fee reconciles with the greater of the STANDARD zone-class fee (SGD 4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00) under POL-NS-01's resolution rule, so POL-NS-08(d) is not engaged. No repeat-dispute pattern exists (both disputes_with_counterparty_90d are 0). The confidence cap is 1.0 - the GPS trace at weight 1.0 is the sole carrier of the deciding fact - so 0.85 sits below the cap."
