    "explanation": "To both parties: the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee (EV-FARE-00212, cancellation_fee line) is refunded to the rider in full, and no driver compensation is payable.\n\nWhy the fee cannot stand. POL-NS-01 lets a no-show fee stand only if all four limbs hold, and limbs (b) and (c) do not. The driver's own trace (EV-GPS-00212) covers the whole waiting window - 93 fixes at 10-second cadence, 100% coverage, no gaps - but against the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius and the 25 m accuracy filter it records 0 qualifying in-geofence fixes and a longest qualifying in-geofence run of 0 seconds. POL-NS-02 says fixes worse than 25 m accuracy count as evidence of neither presence nor absence, so the trace cannot establish an admissible arrival: no qualifying in-radius fix anywhere in the 15 minutes before the 08:20:30 cancellation means the driver never arrived and limb (b) fails, with a full refund. Independently, the waiting clock runs from the first qualifying in-geofence fix, not from the 08:12:35 'arrived' tap (POL-NS-01 limb (c)), so measured dwell is 0 s against the 300 s minimum - a 300 s shortfall - and POL-NS-06 makes the fee non-chargeable and refundable in full whether or not the rider was present. The 7.9 minutes of app wall-time is not dwell.\n\nDriver: your account of being parked at the kerb for nearly eight minutes is not carried by any admissible fix. Your trace shows 3.2 km travelled, a maximum 1082 m from the pin, speeds of 25.2 and 43.5 km/h and no stationary in-geofence interval. Your point that a raw fix came within 37.94 m of the pin does not help: it did not survive the 25 m accuracy filter and counts as evidence of neither presence nor absence. Limb (d) is indeed satisfied - EXCESSIVE_WAIT is one of the three codes POL-NS-01 recognises - but one limb of four does not carry the fee. Your POL-NS-03 wrong-entrance route produces no compensation either: it requires you to have been stationary for the required dwell within 400 m of the pin, which is not shown (and a mean distance of 294 m inside the 400 m corridor is not the test), and in any event registered_pickup_points is 1 and the rider named Exit A in chat, so the pin-ambiguity goodwill limb (ii) cannot apply and limb (i) awards you nothing. POL-NS-07 pays only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, so compensation is nil. For completeness, the anti-farming check does not trip (2 no-show terminations in 30 days, below the absolute threshold of 4, and a rate of 0.015 across 132 completed trips, below 0.08), so POL-NS-09(d) and escalation are not engaged.\n\nRider: your presence at the pin (your track averages 22.6 m and peaks at 40.4 m from it) is confirmed but is not what decides this - POL-NS-06 refunds regardless of rider presence, and POL-NS-04 does not separately exonerate you because the driver answered your 08:15:02 message 28 seconds later, inside its 120-second window.\n\nOn the requested false-arrival record under POL-NS-05(ii): POL-NS-05 fires only where the GPS places the driver more than 300 m from the pin, or moving at 15 km/h or more, at the 08:12:35 arrival-marker timestamp. The computed trace publishes no arrival-matched fix, and a whole-window maximum distance cannot establish the position at the marker, so the false-arrival trigger is not made out and I record no referral on that clause. The refund does not depend on it.\n\nOn integrity and confidence. No artifact is impaired for policy purposes under POL-NS-08(a)-(d): the event and trace timestamps agree to the second, the trace has no gap above 120 s and includes the rider's track, the chat log's four messages match chat_message_count 4 with no missing msg_id, and the SGD 4.00 fee reconciles with the fee_schedule resolution rule - the greater of the SGD 4.00 STANDARD zone-class fee and the SGD 4.00 RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00212-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0), so POL-NS-06(i) accumulation was never available, but nothing turned on it, and citing the missing artifact to establish its own unavailability does not trigger POL-NS-09. Every artifact this ruling rests on carries weight 1.0, so confidence is 0.90, above the 0.70 floor. No profile field outside those the policy names was used as a ground."
